# Google Maps API Key for Android (restricted to org.beanpool.pillar)
# Get a key from Google Cloud Console and paste it here
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=your-api-key-here

# BeanPool's key vault for this build (utils/vault.ts): its address and its public keys, pinned. Public, not secret.
# Ticket keys: 64 hex characters each; deposit keys: base64url; comma-separated, newest first. Leave all three out
# and members' sign-in copies stay at their community, exactly as before the vault; set some but not all and the build
# stops (app.config.js). Until the custodians' parts are reshared, only a TEST vault's values go here: never point a
# real build at a live vault. A vault build is also blocked until (see PR #1336):
#   - CLOSED: the vault signs its releases and deposit receipts (review finding 4): it signs every answer the phone
#     acts on, and the phone acts on no other (utils/vault.ts "Every answer signed");
#   - global's door accepts vault tickets, V5 (finding 5): open until V5's server half is deployed to global with
#     BEANPOOL_VAULT_TICKET_KEYS set. The phone half is in (utils/global-join.ts "Only at a door that takes the
#     ticket"): at a door that doesn't list this build's keys, or refuses the ticket, a vault build joins with the
#     door's own nonce, without a copy, so the gate now decides only whether door joins get a copy;
#   - CLOSED: a member whose only copy is still at a community can get back in (finding 3): on the vault's signed
#     "no copy" for a sign-in, the restore with that provider goes on at the community as a build without a vault does
#     it, and the move card is offered at once (utils/sso-recovery.ts `vaultKeepsNoCopyFor`, kept per provider, not per
#     sign-in account);
#   - CLOSED: a phone told "no copy" learns of a copy the member makes later on another phone (confirmation N1): "no
#     copy" is believed for 7 days, then the app-open check asks again (utils/vault.ts `VAULT_NONE_KEPT_MS`);
#   - CLOSED: a 2xx status answer that isn't a status is not recorded as "no copy" (confirmation N2; utils/vault.ts
#     `vaultStatus`);
#   - the custodians' parts are reshared, and the parked guide pages ship with it (GitHub issue #1349,
#     https://github.com/beanpool-org/beanpool/issues/1349).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BEANPOOL_VAULT_URL=https://vault.example.org
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BEANPOOL_VAULT_TICKET_KEYS=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BEANPOOL_VAULT_DEPOSIT_KEYS=
